{"type":"thinking","text":"The key insight: There is a discrepancy between original-receipt.json (DUTY-2340 at 23:40) and cold-cycle.json (DESK-21 at 21:00). The receipt says limits = [80,40,50,70], actual = [80,40,50,50], departureKwh = [126,121], withinLimits false. The cold-cycle log says limits derived from meter deltas: [80,40,70,50]. Wait let me compute:\n\ncold-cycle samples, each 30 min, meter deltas:\n- slot0: 6040-6000 = 40 kWh / 0.5h = 80 kW\n- slot1: 6060-6040 = 20 kWh / 0.5h = 40 kW\n- slot2: 6095-6060 = 35 kWh / 0.5h = 70 kW\n- slot3: 6120-6095 = 25 kWh / 0.5h = 50 kW\nlimits = [80,40,70,50].\n\nThe plan shift-plan acKw = [80,40,70,50]. So withinLimits true under cold-cycle limits. retest gives actual = [80,40,70,50], departure = [72+0.45*(120)=126, 76+0.45*(120)=130].\n\nBut original-receipt says at a later run DUTY-2340 at 23:40, limits = [80,40,50,70], actual = [80,40,50,50]. So at slot2 (01:00) actual AC is clipped to 50 kW, slot3 (01:30) allowed 70 but requested 50. Thus B's AC energy = (50+50)*0.5=50 kWh, battery gain = 45, departure = 76+45 = 121, margin -9. A = 72 + (80+40)*0.5*0.9 = 126, margin 0.\n\nWait, the original receipt says departureKwh [126,121], withinLimits false. This is the \"current\" record? The desk says \"DESK-21 为 21:00 同班冷夜数字站控台架的交流电表采集，线上参数按适用记录的采集时间生效。本地 node operations/retest.mjs 按这份记录复算。\" The release-format says \"归档的本班原表车辆台架回执见 operations/original-receipt.json，工况与适用范围见单内。调度台名录登记值班维护者，depot_trial 的本席量程为原 21:00 公开采集。\"\n\nHmm. There's a subtlety: which record applies? The original-receipt DUTY-2340 at 23:40 has a later time (23:40) than DESK-21 at 21:00. \"线上参数按适用记录的采集时间生效\" — online parameters take effect by the capture time of the applicable record. But the release-format says \"depot_trial 的本席量程为原 21:00 公开采集\" — depot_trial's local range is the original 21:00 public capture. And \"归档的本班原表车辆台架回执见 operations/original-receipt.json，工况与适用范围见单内\" — archived original sheet vehicle bench receipt. The applicability says: \"站型 R4。站控交流上限按时段固定；四格半小时、两车窗口、20 kW 平移不变时，可将该上限用于窗口内的新设定。90% 工况的车端净增量等于实际交流电量乘 0.90。\" So the limits [80,40,50,70] from the 23:40 receipt apply to the new setting if the slot structure/windows/shift are unchanged. Thus the \"current\" station AC limits are [80,40,50,70], not [80,40,70,50].\n\nThis is the trap: the old cold-cycle at 21:00 gives limits [80,40,70,50], but the later original-receipt at 23:40 records the actual station limits [80,40,50,70], meaning slot 2 is capped at 50 and slot 3 at 70. The plan [80,40,70,50] requests 70 in slot 2, exceeding the 50 limit; station clips to 50, so B gets only 50 kW in slot 2. Thus B departs at 121, 9 short. A is fine. The current plan is not executable as filed because setpoint exceeds slot limit. Need to revise shift-plan.json to stay within [80,40,50,70].\n\nNow can we re-dispatch to get both buses to required levels under actual limits [80,40,50,70] with 20 kW shift? Let's compute capacity per slot (AC charging cap = min(80, 120 - building)). With shifted building [40,80,50,70] (i.e., 20 kW moved from slot1 to slot3): caps = min(80, 120-load):\n- slot0: 120-40=80 -> 80\n- slot1: 120-80=40 -> 40\n- slot2: 120-50=70 -> 70 (but station limit at slot2 is 50)\n- slot3: 120-70=50 -> 50 (station limit slot3 70, so 50)\n\nBut actual site limits per slot: [80,40,50,70]. So effective caps = [min(80,80), min(40,40), min(70,50), min(50,70)] = [80,40,50,50]. A window slots 0,1: max AC = (80+40)*0.5 = 60 kWh, battery gain 54, exactly 126. B window slots 2,3: (50+50)*0.5 = 50 kWh, battery gain 45, departure 121. Deficit 9. Can we shift more from slot1? Slot1 building cold is 100 originally (80+20). With 20 shift it's 80, cap 40. If we shift more (maxShiftKw 40), slot1 load reduces further, cap increases up to 80 if load <= 40, but that requires 60 shift > max 40. At shift 40, slot1 load = 60, cap = 60. Hmm, but A window already has enough? A needs exactly 54 battery = 60 AC. At shift 20, A gets 60 AC exactly. Shifting more from slot1 to slot3 would increase A's available capacity but A only needs 60 AC; extra can't help B because B window starts slot2. Could shift from slot2 to slot3? No, shiftFromSlot=1, shiftToSlot=3 fixed. Only 20 kW appointment already made? \"20 kW 平移已预约\" — 20 kW shift is reserved. The rules say only from shiftFromSlot to shiftToSlot, maxShiftKw 40. But the task says \"排班保持现有字段、两车时窗、20 kW 已预约平移和高效工况下最大可用充电量\" — keep existing fields, two-car windows, 20 kW reserved shift, and maximum usable charging amount under high-efficiency conditions. So we keep loadShiftKw = 20, not increase. Thus B is inherently 9 short under actual limits. Hmm wait, maybe we can reallocate charging power: B could charge in slot 2 at 50 and slot3 at 50 = 100 AC = 90 battery, required 54 battery gain -> B needs 54/0.9 = 60 AC. Wait, B's required is 130, start 76, needs 54 battery = 60 AC. B gets 100 AC available from [50,50]? Wait, (50+50) kW * 0.5 h = 50 kWh AC, not 100. I conflated. Let's recompute: caps are kW. Each slot 0.5 h. slot2 50 kW * 0.5 = 25 kWh; slot3 50 kW * 0.5 = 25 kWh; total 50 kWh AC -> 45 kWh battery. B needs 54 kWh battery -> 9 short. Yes.\n\nBut wait, could B charge at slot3 up to 70 kW if we shift building load away from slot3? The 20 kW shift adds to slot3, raising building from 50 to 70, so cap = 50. If we shift less to slot3, slot3 cap would be higher, but then slot1 cap lower hurting A. Maybe a different shift between 0 and 20 could balance? Let's think: A's window is slots 0,1. A needs 60 AC. At shift s from slot1 to slot3, building slot1 = 100 - s, cap1 = min(80, 120-(100-s)) = min(80, 20+s). building slot3 = 50 + s, cap3 = min(80, 120-(50+s)) = min(80, 70-s). With station limits slot1 = 40, slot3 = 70.\n\nEffective cap1 = min(20+s, 40) = 20+s for s<=20; cap3 = min(70-s, 70) = 70-s for s<=20. A's max AC = 0.5*(cap0 + cap1) = 0.5*(80 + 20+s) = 50 + s/2 kWh. Need 60 -> s >= 20. So exactly s=20 for A. B's max AC = 0.5*(cap2 + cap3), cap2 = min(80,120-50=70, station 50)=50; cap3 = min(70-s,70). At s=20, cap3=50. B AC = 0.5*(50+50)=50; need 60. deficit 10 AC = 9 battery. So under actual limits, no feasible s<=20. If s>20 (up to 40), A's cap1 = 40 (station limit) once 20+s>=40 (s>=20), A max = 60 AC; B cap3 = 70-s <50, so B gets worse. So B max at s=0: cap3 = 70 (station limit), cap2 = 50 -> B AC = 60, exactly need 60; but then A cap1 = 20 -> A AC = 0.5*(80+20) = 50, needs 60 -> A short 10 AC (9 battery). So you can't satisfy both simultaneously with 20 kW shift under actual limits. Interesting: A and B each need 60 AC, total 120 AC. Total effective capacity over 4 slots = 0.5*(80+40+50+70) = 0.5*240 = 120 AC. Exactly enough total, but windows disjoint and shift constraints make allocation: A can use slot0 80 and slot1 only 20+s; B slot2 50 and slot3 70-s. Sum required: A needs 60, B needs 60. At s=20, A=60, B=50. At s=0, A=50, B=60. There's a tradeoff of 1 kWh per kW shift? Actually shifting 1 kW from slot1 to slot3: A loses 0.5 kWh AC, B gains 0.5 kWh AC. Total constant at 120. So cannot give both 60 unless s such that A=60 and B=60 simultaneously -> requires 50+s/2=60 => s=20; B=0.5*(50+70-20)=50. Not both. So no way with this station limit and 20 kW shift? Wait, could B use slot2 at more than 50 by reducing building load in slot2? The only allowed shift is slot1->slot3. No.\n\nBut maybe the \"actual limits\" aren't fixed per slot; maybe the original receipt's limits [80,40,50,70] represent actual AC meter readings for the *old setting* and the applicability says \"站控交流上限按时段固定\" — the station control AC limits are fixed by time slot, so yes fixed. The station clips actual power to the limit. So new setpoint can't exceed. Thus current sheet [80,40,70,50] is not executable. Need revis","truncated":true}
